course: dictionary
lesson: 12156
title: Complainant: the person who complains
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A complainant is a person who makes an official complaint, or brings a case to a court, saying they have been wronged. A complaint is a formal way of saying something is wrong. The complainant is the person who makes it.
explain: The word is built from complain and the ending -ant, which often means a person who does something. «The complainant said the shop had sold her a broken bike.» Here the complainant is the shopper, the person who says she was treated unfairly.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Court, lawyer, letter and formal are all signs that the word is about an official matter. «The complainant's lawyer read the letter to the court.» Swap in "the person who complained" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A complainant is a person who makes a formal complaint.
fact: In law, a complainant brings a case to a court and says they have been wronged.
fact: A complaint can also be made to a company or a school, not only to a court.
fact: The ending -ant often means a person who does something, so complainant is "one who complains".
fact: Clue words such as court, lawyer, formal and official often show that a complainant is involved.
exercise: «The complainant said the shop had sold her a broken bike.» What is a complainant? | A shop that sells bikes | *A person who makes a formal complaint about being wronged | A bike that is broken | A lawyer who works in a court
exercise: «The complainant's lawyer read the letter to the court.» Find and copy one word that tells you this is a legal matter. | lawyer's | letter | *court | read
exercise: Ella says a complainant is just another word for a friend. Why is she wrong? | A complainant is a friend who helps you | *A complainant is someone who makes a formal complaint about being wronged | A complainant is a lawyer who speaks for people | A complainant is a shop owner
test: «Ben, the complainant, wrote to the school about the bullying.» Who is Ben? | A teacher who writes the school reports | *A person who made a formal complaint to the school | A headteacher who wrote a letter home | A child who has just moved to a new school
test: «The complainant waited outside the court while the case was heard.» What is the complainant in this sentence? | The judge who decides the case | The court clerk who writes things down | *The person who made the complaint | The building where the trial takes place
exam: A complainant is best described as: | A type of bread roll | A person who has never complained about anything | *A person who makes a formal complaint, saying they have been wronged | A small room in a court
